In Python, a class is a blueprint for creating objects. You can define a class as follows:
class Person:
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age
    def greet(self):
        print(f'Hi, I am {self.name} and I am {self.age} years old.')

Simple class example:
class Animal:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
    def speak(self):
        print(f'{self.name} makes a sound.')

A method is a function that belongs to a class. You can define a method as follows:
class Car:
    def __init__(self, brand, model):
        self.brand = brand
        self.model = model
    def drive(self):
        print(f'The car {self.brand} {self.model} is driving.')

The `__init__` method initializes object attributes when it is created:
class Book:
    def __init__(self, title, author):
        self.title = title
        self.author = author
book1 = Book('1984', 'George Orwell')

Inheritance allows one class to inherit attributes and methods from another. Example:
class Animal:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
    def speak(self):
        print(f'{self.name} makes a sound.')
class Dog(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        print(f'{self.name} barks.')

Polymorphism allows a method to behave differently in different classes. Example:
class Animal:
    def speak(self):
        pass
class Dog(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        print('The dog barks.')
class Cat(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        print('The cat meows.')

Encapsulation allows you to hide internal details of a class. In Python, private attributes are indicated with double underscores. Example:
class Person:
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.__name = name  # Private attribute
        self.__age = age  # Private attribute
    def get_name(self):
        return self.__name

Abstraction allows you to define a base class with abstract methods that must be implemented by child classes. Example using `abc` (Abstract Base Class):
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod
class Animal(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def speak(self):
        pass
class Dog(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        print('The dog barks.')

